  "prefLabel": "Nur 102.02 Organization",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Nur 102.02 Organization.\n\n(a) The board shall be comprised of 13 members who meet the applicable eligibility requirements of RSA 326-B:3, II to VI, and are appointed pursuant to RSA 326-B:3, VIII.\n\n(b) As required by RSA 326-B:3, I, membership of the board shall include:\n\n(1) Six registered nurses, 2 of which are advanced practice registered nurses;\n\n(2) Two licensed practical nurses;\n\n(3) Three licensed nursing assistants, one of which is a medication licensed nursing assistant, if possible; and\n\n(4) Two public members.\n\n(c) The board shall form standing or ad hoc committees to accomplish the board’s functions.\n\n(d) In December every 2 years, the board shall elect one member to serve as chair and one member to serve as vice chair and shall serve as follows:\n\n(1) The chair shall preside over the board’s meetings, establish the order of its business, and approve the actions of the administrator, consistent with the policies of the OPLC; and\n\n(2) The vice-chair shall assume the duties of the chair in their absence.\n\n(e) No member of the board shall serve as chair or vice-chair of the board more than one consecutive 2 year term. The vice-chair shall be authorized to move to the chair position for an additional 2 year term if the board chooses to elect that individual as chair.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Nur 100) #5887, eff 8-26-94; ss by #6778, eff 6-26-98; ss by #7736, eff 8-6-02; ss by #8777, eff 12-23-06; ss by #10296, eff 3-22-13; ss by #10569, eff 4-17-14; amd by #11144, eff 7-28-16; ss by #14294, eff 6-27-25",
